{"version":3,"kind":"Article","sha256":"b9063eabfe9fe0b762393fbfe5ca50e1cb0eff2610a8addbd2a13a7b73c74b9e","slug":"book.paper-notes.2022-01-01-productivity-spillovers-compensation","location":"/book/paper-notes/2022-01-01-productivity-spillovers-compensation.md","dependencies":[],"frontmatter":{"title":"Productivity spillovers and the productivity-compensation gap","description":"Accounting for spatial and trade-network productivity spillovers narrows the productivity-compensation gap in some industries but effects vary significantly.","short_title":"Productivity spillovers and compensation","tags":["labor","regional-economics","spillovers"],"date":"2022-01-01","content_includes_title":false,"copyright":"2026","numbering":{"title":{"offset":1}},"exports":[{"format":"md","filename":"2022-01-01-productivity-spillovers-compensation.md","url":"/build/2022-01-01-productiv-26e6600a3c35d89af8a3762102939b41.md"}]},"mdast":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"block","children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":14,"column":1},"end":{"line":15,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":14,"column":1},"end":{"line":14,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Publication id","position":{"start":{"line":14,"column":1},"end":{"line":14,"column":1}},"key":"hZ8abLcJTb"}],"key":"YJ3xBHp6N1"},{"type":"text","value":": ","position":{"start":{"line":14,"column":1},"end":{"line":14,"column":1}},"key":"HyfJNridEN"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"shakya-2022-productivity-spillovers-compensation","position":{"start":{"line":14,"column":1},"end":{"line":14,"column":1}},"key":"EpKXAJVHhM"},{"type":"break","position":{"start":{"line":14,"column":1},"end":{"line":14,"column":1}},"key":"aLiYdH7xMU"},{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":14,"column":1},"end":{"line":14,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Status","position":{"start":{"line":14,"column":1},"end":{"line":14,"column":1}},"key":"yDGpHvLMez"}],"key":"gKKISlGfzg"},{"type":"text","value":": verified","position":{"start":{"line":14,"column":1},"end":{"line":14,"column":1}},"key":"pSljwhr8pO"}],"key":"vlK9eL9DRl"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":17,"column":1},"end":{"line":17,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":17,"column":1},"end":{"line":17,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Citation","position":{"start":{"line":17,"column":1},"end":{"line":17,"column":1}},"key":"DMMPJl8Y5a"}],"key":"zPZlxAiwtS"},{"type":"text","value":": Shakya, S., & Plemmons, A. (2022). Productivity spillovers and the productivity-compensation gap. ","position":{"start":{"line":17,"column":1},"end":{"line":17,"column":1}},"key":"vnHyCZZ7KU"},{"type":"emphasis","position":{"start":{"line":17,"column":1},"end":{"line":17,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Spatial Economic Analysis","position":{"start":{"line":17,"column":1},"end":{"line":17,"column":1}},"key":"WeVKIB6hVF"}],"key":"vQD9st7S06"},{"type":"text","value":". ","position":{"start":{"line":17,"column":1},"end":{"line":17,"column":1}},"key":"PcYXBr84po"},{"type":"link","url":"https://www.dropbox.com/scl/fi/0hspku758et24sw781ara/Shakya-Plemmons-SEA-2022.pdf?rlkey=y5ndrb1jilznbzzwfyxkmkdwa&dl=0","position":{"start":{"line":17,"column":1},"end":{"line":17,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Download PDF","position":{"start":{"line":17,"column":1},"end":{"line":17,"column":1}},"key":"JMthqG9UDd"}],"urlSource":"https://www.dropbox.com/scl/fi/0hspku758et24sw781ara/Shakya-Plemmons-SEA-2022.pdf?rlkey=y5ndrb1jilznbzzwfyxkmkdwa&dl=0","key":"I5ECqn1Aut"}],"key":"aHF4ugCeF9"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":19,"column":1},"end":{"line":19,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Facts","position":{"start":{"line":19,"column":1},"end":{"line":19,"column":1}},"key":"mz6LX6Vjj1"}],"identifier":"facts","label":"Facts","html_id":"facts","implicit":true,"key":"d3DzIK4ZoL"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"position":{"start":{"line":21,"column":1},"end":{"line":21,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Policy hook","position":{"start":{"line":21,"column":1},"end":{"line":21,"column":1}},"key":"hKtGMckZkR"}],"identifier":"policy-hook","label":"Policy hook","html_id":"policy-hook","implicit":true,"key":"jsrJlg5QRW"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":23,"column":1},"end":{"line":23,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Since the 1970s, US worker productivity has grown faster than wage growth—a divergence called the productivity-compensation gap. Conventional explanations focus on within-firm dynamics, but recent economics emphasizes spillovers: productivity gains in one region may benefit workers elsewhere through trade and knowledge diffusion. Does accounting for these cross-regional spillovers explain part of the gap?","position":{"start":{"line":23,"column":1},"end":{"line":23,"column":1}},"key":"JtvbYrRQN4"}],"key":"DBkC4egDn8"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"position":{"start":{"line":25,"column":1},"end":{"line":25,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Main finding","position":{"start":{"line":25,"column":1},"end":{"line":25,"column":1}},"key":"qkTGaoDyle"}],"identifier":"main-finding","label":"Main finding","html_id":"main-finding","implicit":true,"key":"wCjy4F9kDp"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":27,"column":1},"end":{"line":27,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The productivity-compensation gap narrows significantly in some industries once productivity spillovers between bordering and trading states are accounted for using spatially lagged models. However, effects are heterogeneous across the 23 industries examined—gap reduction is not uniform, with substantial variation in how spillovers mediate the relationship between productivity and compensation.","position":{"start":{"line":27,"column":1},"end":{"line":27,"column":1}},"key":"eVRMBZe7Ad"}],"key":"mBJq2ISb9d"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"position":{"start":{"line":29,"column":1},"end":{"line":29,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Data and setting","position":{"start":{"line":29,"column":1},"end":{"line":29,"column":1}},"key":"sa4RpVRYiI"}],"identifier":"data-and-setting","label":"Data and setting","html_id":"data-and-setting","implicit":true,"key":"jNDhUgMR2o"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":31,"column":1},"end":{"line":31,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"IO-Snap state-level industry data on employment, compensation, and gross industrial output (2012); Commodity Flow Survey Public Use Microdata File containing approximately 4.5 million shipments for interstate trade analysis; analysis covers 23 industries across all 50 US states.","position":{"start":{"line":31,"column":1},"end":{"line":31,"column":1}},"key":"vySeu49oI7"}],"key":"TfD0VA1mXp"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"position":{"start":{"line":33,"column":1},"end":{"line":33,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Research design (plain language)","position":{"start":{"line":33,"column":1},"end":{"line":33,"column":1}},"key":"SyUhVegWEw"}],"identifier":"research-design-plain-language","label":"Research design (plain language)","html_id":"research-design-plain-language","implicit":true,"key":"Q0uP9SXBZn"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":35,"column":1},"end":{"line":35,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Spatial econometrics using Spatially Lagged X (SLX) models examining two dimensions of spillovers: spatial (contiguous states) and trade-network (trading states). Compares baseline models to spatially-adjusted specifications. Instrumental variables approach addresses endogeneity concerns. Log-log regression specifications allow comparison of productivity-compensation linkages across industries.","position":{"start":{"line":35,"column":1},"end":{"line":35,"column":1}},"key":"DjSGAR0w1i"}],"key":"wLJeWUAK2P"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"position":{"start":{"line":37,"column":1},"end":{"line":37,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"One caveat","position":{"start":{"line":37,"column":1},"end":{"line":37,"column":1}},"key":"UKLRxyjEYp"}],"identifier":"one-caveat","label":"One caveat","html_id":"one-caveat","implicit":true,"key":"QPaF8FUd2k"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":39,"column":1},"end":{"line":39,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Results vary significantly across industries and model specifications; not all industries show gap reduction when accounting for spillovers. Uses single-year cross-sectional data (2012), limiting temporal analysis. Geographic and trade network definitions are static, potentially missing dynamic spillover patterns over time or across business cycles.","position":{"start":{"line":39,"column":1},"end":{"line":39,"column":1}},"key":"NXQ0y5tdur"}],"key":"JAv8h136ST"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"position":{"start":{"line":41,"column":1},"end":{"line":41,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"PDF or DOI","position":{"start":{"line":41,"column":1},"end":{"line":41,"column":1}},"key":"GCBhy25ofe"}],"identifier":"pdf-or-doi","label":"PDF or DOI","html_id":"pdf-or-doi","implicit":true,"key":"qp9yut6QAC"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":43,"column":1},"end":{"line":43,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"link","url":"https://www.dropbox.com/scl/fi/0hspku758et24sw781ara/Shakya-Plemmons-SEA-2022.pdf?rlkey=y5ndrb1jilznbzzwfyxkmkdwa&dl=0","position":{"start":{"line":43,"column":1},"end":{"line":43,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Download PDF","position":{"start":{"line":43,"column":1},"end":{"line":43,"column":1}},"key":"T1ZtYT2sC2"}],"urlSource":"https://www.dropbox.com/scl/fi/0hspku758et24sw781ara/Shakya-Plemmons-SEA-2022.pdf?rlkey=y5ndrb1jilznbzzwfyxkmkdwa&dl=0","key":"eretp6qbSi"}],"key":"MkgVzGza37"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":45,"column":1},"end":{"line":45,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Why it matters","position":{"start":{"line":45,"column":1},"end":{"line":45,"column":1}},"key":"fAKedPc4fy"}],"identifier":"why-it-matters","label":"Why it matters","html_id":"why-it-matters","implicit":true,"key":"xfqXmu65Fk"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":47,"column":1},"end":{"line":47,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The productivity-compensation gap is a central inequality story: workers are more productive but wages stagnate. Explanations range from technology replacing labor to corporate rent-seeking. This paper suggests that geographic spillovers matter—productivity gains in neighboring or trading states may accrue to capital owners there rather than being shared with workers. For policymakers, the finding implies that local wage-setting cannot ignore regional productivity dynamics. Industries integrated through trade networks face different incentives than isolated sectors. For labor advocates, it suggests that wage policy may need regional coordination rather than local-only approaches. The heterogeneity across industries also indicates that productivity-compensation dynamics vary by sector, implying that sector-specific policy design may be more effective than economy-wide solutions.","position":{"start":{"line":47,"column":1},"end":{"line":47,"column":1}},"key":"x7sNwt3vrS"}],"key":"drhjFVqitI"}],"key":"fr00CLlPkE"}],"key":"n1KBeYidUW"},"references":{"cite":{"order":[],"data":{}}},"footer":{"navigation":{"prev":{"title":"Shale revolution, oil and gas prices, and drilling","short_title":"Shale revolution and drilling","url":"/book/paper-notes/2022-01-01-shale-revolution-drilling","group":"Publications"},"next":{"title":"Nurse licensure compact and mobility","short_title":"Nurse licensure compact mobility","url":"/book/paper-notes/2022-01-01-nurse-licensure-compact-mobility","group":"Publications"}}},"domain":"http://localhost:3000"}